    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "A continuously active or relict landform pattern built up to the present sea level, or that of a former time, by corals and other organisms. It is mainly level, with moderately inclined to precipitous slopes below sea level. Stream channels are generally absent, but there may occasionally be fixed deep erosional tidal stream channels forming a disintegrated non-tributary pattern.",
